---
/**
 * Privacy notice (App_Flow §A.1; PRD Rules 9, 13, 14, 15, NV1, NV2). LegalLayout, no ads.
 * Each statement describes what the code does: project data and theme in localStorage,
 * one consent cookie, Cloudflare Web Analytics and Google AdSense only after consent.
 *
 * LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED before launch (Engineering_Plan: agent audit items). A qualified
 * person should check the regional wording (UK GDPR, EU GDPR, CCPA and similar), the
 * operator's name and address, and the retention and rights sections. Also set
 * PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL.
 */
import ConsentButton from '../components/common/ConsentButton.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const description =
  'What Beautally stores, what it never sends, and how analytics and advertising work only after you say yes.';
const { contactEmail } = SITE;
---

<LegalLayout title="Privacy notice" description={description} path="/privacy/" updated="2026-11-15">
  <p class="text-lg">
    Beautally is built so your rooms stay on your device. This page explains what is stored, what is
    shared, and the choices you have.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your rooms, sizes and prices are saved in your browser. We never receive them.</li>
    <li>There are no accounts and no sign-up.</li>
    <li>Analytics and advertising are off until you accept them.</li>
    <li>You can delete your saved rooms at any time with Clear my data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is saved on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Your project is saved in your browser's local storage, under one key. It holds the rooms you
    add, their sizes and openings, and your material options. It also holds any prices you type and
    your region and unit choice.
  </p>
  <p>
    A second item remembers whether you prefer the light or dark theme. A third, a small cookie
    named beautally_consent, remembers your cookie choices for about six months.
  </p>
  <p>
    None of this is sent to us or to anyone else. It stays on your device until you remove it. Clear
    my data deletes your project. Clearing your browser's site data removes everything.
  </p>

  <h2>What we receive</h2>
  <p>
    Beautally has no server of its own that stores your data. The site is delivered by Cloudflare.
    Like any website host, Cloudflare receives your IP address and basic request details when it
    sends you a page.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not combine this with your rooms, because we never see your rooms. We do not sell personal
    information.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics, only if you accept</h2>
  <p>
    If analytics is switched on and you accept it, we use Cloudflare Web Analytics. It counts page
    visits and measures how fast pages load. It is designed to work without cookies.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may also count simple actions, such as a list being printed. These counts carry values like
    your region, your unit system and the number of rooms. They never carry a room name or a
    measurement.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising, only if you accept</h2>
  <p>
    Beautally may show ads from Google AdSense. No ad code is loaded until you accept advertising.
    If you accept, Google and its partners may set cookies or use identifiers to show and measure
    ads.
  </p>
  <p>
    Read how Google uses information from sites that use its services at{' '}
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">
      policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites
    </a>
    . Ads never appear in the room form or in your results, and they cannot see your rooms.
  </p>

  <h2>Shop links</h2>
  <p>
    Some links may take you to a shop. If so, they are marked as sponsored. When you follow one,
    that shop learns you came from Beautally, and its own privacy policy applies. We do not pass on
    your measurements.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Change your cookie choices at any time with the button below, or from the footer.</li>
    <li>Delete your saved rooms with Clear my data.</li>
    <li>Block or delete cookies and site data in your browser settings.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <ConsentButton label="Open cookie preferences" />
  </p>
  <p>
    Read more about cookies in the <a href="/cookies/">cookie notice</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    The law where you live may give you rights over personal information. You may be able to ask to
    see, correct or delete it. We keep no personal information about you, so there is usually
    nothing for us to give, correct or delete.
  </p>
  <p>If you think we hold something about you, write to us and we will look into it.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Beautally is made for adults planning home projects. It is not aimed at children, and we do not
    knowingly collect information from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    If we change how Beautally handles data, we will update this page and its date. The date at the
    top shows when it last changed.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy? Write to us at
    {contactEmail ? (
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
    ) : (
      <span>[contact address to be added before launch]</span>
    )}
    .
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
